3. NVIDIA MathDx / cuFFTDx, and GPU builds
------------------------------------------

Status. No MathDx or cuFFTDx file is in this repository or in any release
asset. qefast/sth/fdx/deps.sh fetches the
nvidia-mathdx package from PyPI at build time, and only when a user runs it.
qefast/sth/fdx/sth_fftdx.cu is qe-fast's own code, GPL-licensed. It uses the
public cuFFTDx API and contains no NVIDIA sample code.

Terms. MathDx is proprietary: "LICENSE AGREEMENT FOR NVIDIA MATH LIBRARIES
SOFTWARE DEVELOPMENT KITS" (v. February 10, 2022), as shipped with
nvidia-mathdx 25.6.0. Whoever downloads it accepts that agreement. Section 2.6
reads: "You may not use the SDK in any manner that would cause it to become
subject to an open source software license", with examples of licences that
require the SDK to be disclosed or distributed in source code form, licensed
for making derivative works, or redistributable at no charge. Section 1.2(v)
requires the terms of a distributed application to be consistent with the
agreement.

The conflict. cuFFTDx is a C++ header library. Its code is instantiated into
the kernels in the object file, and that object file is linked into ph.x and
epw.x. Distributing such a binary would require offering the complete
corresponding source under the GPL (sections 2 and 3), which the NVIDIA terms
do not allow for MathDx. It cannot satisfy both. The GPL's system-library
exception does not plausibly help: MathDx is a separately downloaded SDK whose
code is compiled into the program. A linking exception is not a way out either,
since it would have to come from all the copyright holders of Quantum ESPRESSO.

Position.
- The source code in this repository can be distributed under the GPL. It
  contains no NVIDIA MathDx code.
- Building with MathDx for your own use involves no distribution, so the GPL
  places no condition on it.
- DO NOT distribute a binary, container image or other package built with
  QEF_MATHDX_INC set. The qe-fast project does not publish any.
- The build works without MathDx. When QEF_MATHDX_INC and QEF_CUTLASS_INC are
  not both set, CMake compiles qefast/sth/fdx/sth_fftdx_stub.c instead. The stub
  always declines, so the run keeps cuFFT and loses only the gain of the
  cuFFTDx kernels. CPU builds never touch this code.

Other GPU build dependencies. Every GPU build, of upstream QE as well, links
NVIDIA's proprietary runtime libraries (CUDA, cuFFT, cuBLAS and the NVHPC
runtime). Those are dynamically linked and are not compiled into the program,
and whether the GPL's system-library exception covers them is a question that
anyone distributing GPU binaries should answer with their own legal advice.
